  "Question": "A spring has an initial length of 10 cm and extends by 0.5 cm for every 1 kg hung from it. Write the relationship between the spring's length \\(L\\) and the mass \\(m\\). Which of the following is correct?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(L=0.5m\\)",
    "B": "\\(L=10m+0.5\\)",
    "C": "\\(L=10-0.5m\\)",
    "D": "\\(L=10+0.5m\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Length = initial length + extension. The extension is \\(0.5m\\), so \\(L=10+0.5m\\).",
